<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1386">1386</a>–<a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Raad van Vlaanderen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> was the high court and governing council of the County of Flanders, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-bold">Philip the Bold</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, in 1386. Seated first at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a> and later at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, it heard appeals and cases touching the count's rights and supervised local justice. It survived under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as the county's supreme court until the French annexation of 1795.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-flanders.jpg" alt="Council of Flanders" width="290" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raad_van_vlaanderen.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
